        {
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is NAS 410 certification issued by ASNT or by my employer?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "By your employer. NAS 410 is an employer-based scheme: the employer, acting through a designated Responsible Level 3, evaluates your training and experience, administers or accepts the examinations, and signs the certificate. ASNT publishes SNT-TC-1A and operates its own central certification programmes, but it does not issue NAS 410 certificates. No training provider can issue one either, whatever their marketing says."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Can NAS 410 formal training hours be delivered online?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The standard controls content, instructor approval and hour count rather than delivery medium, so the Responsible Level 3 decides whether a given online course satisfies the written practice. The constraint is practical: the practical examination must be conducted hands-on with real equipment and representative aerospace specimens, and trainee experience hours are accumulated on actual production work. Classroom theory can be remote; the qualification cannot be completed remotely."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does NAS 410 treat digital radiography as a separate method from film?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Rev 5 splits radiography into film-or-non-film and film-and-non-film in its training and experience tables. A technician qualified in one modality alone follows the 40-hour Level 1 and 40-hour Level 2 route with 800 direct-entry experience hours. A technician qualified in both follows the 60 and 60 route with 1,000 experience hours. For techniques such as phased array ultrasonics, the employer's written practice defines technique-level qualification on top of the method."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What has to be in a NAS 410 certification file?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Identification of the individual and the employer, the method and level certified, the education, training and experience record with hours and sources, examination results broken out by general, specific and practical plus the composite score, the signature or identification of the certifying authority, current near-vision and colour differentiation records, and the certification and expiry dates. Missing or undated vision records are among the most frequently cited deficiencies."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does military or aviation maintenance experience count toward NAS 410 experience hours?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Prior experience counts to the extent it is documented, verifiable and in the specific method being certified. The receiving employer's Responsible Level 3 assesses the evidence, credits what qualifies against the Table 2 minimums, and determines what remains. Military NDT service records and A&P maintenance logs are frequently strong evidence, but general aviation maintenance time that did not involve the method itself does not count toward that method's hours."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Do I need a NAS 410 Level 3 on staff, or can I contract one?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Either works, provided the arrangement is written. Where an employer has no in-house Level 3, it may authorize an outside agency in writing to discharge all or part of the Level 3 responsibilities on a contractual basis. The employer still issues the certificates and retains ultimate responsibility. Atlantis provides outsourced ASNT Level III coverage on that basis; contact us at /contact or info@atlantisndt.com."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
