                "text": "QuickBooks owns tax. The ERP sends taxable status and jurisdiction per line; QuickBooks computes the tax with its own rate tables so the filed return and the posted invoice always agree. Computing tax in the ERP and pushing a total invites penny-level mismatches that block reconciliation."
