                "text": "They are twin standards maintained in technical harmony — NAS 410 by the Aerospace Industries Association in the US, EN 4179 by ASD in Europe. Requirements track each other closely, and multinational programs accept certification to either. The practical difference is oversight: EN 4179 operates with national aerospace NDT boards, while US programs run on employer certification under prime-customer and Nadcap audit."
