                "text": "As corroborating evidence, yes; as the log, no. A timesheet proves presence and duration but records no method, technique, equipment, procedure or supervising certificate holder — five of the seven fields a compliant entry needs. Pair timesheets with inspection reports during reconstruction; going forward, log method-level detail at the point of work."
