                "text": "Both are contracted rather than employed. An interim engagement is time-boxed to an event — an audit, a vacancy, a certification cycle — and ends on a stated date with a handoff package. A standing outside Level III arrangement is ongoing with no terminal date. The authority limits are identical in both cases: the employer remains the certifying authority."
