                "text": "No, and the distinction is the whole reason outsourced Level IIIs exist. The ASNT certificate attests that an individual passed third-party basic and method examinations. Employer certification is separate: under SNT-TC-1A and NAS 410 the employer certifies its own personnel against its own written practice, and needs a qualified Level III to write that practice and administer the examinations. The certificate qualifies the person to hold the role. The written practice is what actually certifies your technicians."
