                "text": "The examinations performed after the lapse date are the ones in question, not the whole job. That is why point-in-time records matter: you have to show which examinations fall either side of the boundary. A dispatch gate that evaluates the projected job end date, not only the start date, prevents the situation from arising on multi-week turnarounds."
